think Opened with the scoped cold roster pass and held still while it ran, reading only. It came back run_verdict=guard_red at 129 guards, 125 green, 2 red, 2 gated, 983s: fleet_watch red 25s, and standing_equipment red beneath it reading `red: fleet_watch red`. Reds first, so the constructive lap I had drafted waited.
think The evidence file for fleet_watch held SEVEN lines -- three banner says, one progress say, and an assertion whose entire diagnostic was `pass=15 fail=1`. Then the control passed 16 of 16 alone, and again five more times. A flake, and the one reading that could have told me WHICH of sixteen behaviors slipped was missing.
think Read the control rather than guessing. tools/fixtures/f/fleet_watch_control.sh line 24 prints `FAIL %s -- wanted %s, got %s` to STDERR so a passing run stays quiet, and tools/f/fleet_watch_witness.rish line 17 interpolates ${ctl.out} and never ${ctl.err}. The exit code travels, the summary travels, the clause naming the behavior does not.
think Measured the class before repairing it. Eight tracked controls print FAIL to stderr; five of the eight are run by a witness; all five of those witnesses stood on the standing roster interpolating .out alone -- fleet_watch, fleet_lap_verdict, publish_template, unshared_citation, sealed_digest. That is a loom rather than a lantern, so it earns an instrument.
think Proved the repair on metal before believing it: planted one wrong expected value in sealed_digest_control.sh, ran the witness, and the evidence went from `pass=8 fail=1` alone to that line plus `FAIL an unread seal is counted -- wanted PLANTED_WRONG, got yes`. Restored the control and checked it byte-identical with cmp.
think Widened shim_reason rather than writing a second guard. One law -- hand on your target's reason -- and two shapes: its three-mark reading requires `say r.out` and `exit r.code`, which is a pass-through shim, where these are witnesses that assert.
obs A FLAKE IS EXACTLY WHEN THE SENTENCE MATTERS MOST, and that is the half worth carrying. A reproducible red can be re-run until it explains itself; a red that will not reproduce is diagnosable only from what it wrote down the first time. So the guards most in need of a forwarded reason are precisely the ones whose reds are hardest to reproduce -- and this one had six clean re-runs to prove it.
obs THE READING CAUGHT ITSELF, which is the case I would keep if I could keep only one. My control's pen helper WRITES a stderr-reporting control into a pen, so its own source carries that line inside single quotes -- and the population count jumped 8 to 9, the instrument counting as one of its own subjects. That is this guard's own roster-anchor lesson (a path in a comment is prose, not a seat) met one reading over, in the same hour, by the same hand that had just written the anchor into its block. The population is anchored on what stands immediately before the command now, and both spellings of a mention are planted -- with the quoted plant reproducing the real continuation-line shape rather than something near it, because a first draft put a live printf and a quoted mention on ONE line, which is genuinely ambiguous and is not the fault I fixed. A plant must be the fault, not something near it.
obs AND THE CONTROL CAUGHT A HOLE IN ITSELF TOO, one lane over. The catalog control's innocence leg patches a copy of the scan and proves the patch landed with `cmp -s` -- and when I first ran it from the wrong directory the source was unreadable, the copy came out EMPTY, cmp said they differ, and the leg reported `innocence patch landed`. An empty copy differs from the original exactly as a real patch does. Emptiness is checked before difference now. REDS `%519`'s law says prove the plant landed; this says prove it landed with something in it.
obs THE ROTA EARNED ITS SEAT, plainly. Lap 4114, row 4, Earth -- the row that breathes in, whose Dual seat is `the-marked-value`, whose Amber clause promises a reader in another decade knows what the cellar held without opening it. I read that and then read my own lane's cellar: bron-resins/manifest.bron named 3 of 17 resins, the habit its own note line states lapsed after one morning on `20260712`, and nothing in the tree had ever read the file. Eighty-seven days of a catalog that reads exactly like a whole one.
obs I MEASURED THE CLASS BEFORE BUILDING FOR IT, and the measurement said build small. Every tracked file in a living room whose name carries manifest, catalog, or roster, crossed with its readers: the mycelium corpora have a witness and a Rye reader apiece, forge_cellar_manifest is read by pond/apps/drawn_terminal.rye, the seat rosters by twenty, nine, and eight sites. bron-resins/manifest.bron was the one enumeration of a room with no reader at all. A lantern, so one cellar's scan rather than a general instrument -- and the near-miss named rather than swept up: cellar/ring1_manifest_shape.bron is cited only by its own README and is a shape rather than an enumeration, in a lane I do not hold.
obs THE CARD ARRIVED AT 40,959 OF 40,960 -- one byte under. My first block was 1,147 bytes against the 506 it replaced, and no amount of tightening two CLOSED accounts fits 1,147 into 507. The seated answer is the card's own: landed accounts shelve like REDS rows, so the account went whole to a shelf and the card carries three lines and a link. Worth naming as a fleet fact rather than a personal one: a pin one byte under its ceiling taxes every lap a condense, and eight ships write this file.
obs THE PIN WENT OVER AND I FOLDED RATHER THAN TRIMMED. Two new rows took REDS.md from 38,703 to 46,574 against 40,960. Four foldable rows -- three BOOKED, one CLOSED -- went oldest-first to one shelf through reds_fold.sh, which re-anchors links and writes the recital, and the pin reads 37,501 with 3,459 of headroom. Every OPEN row stayed where a reader meets it, which is the rule.
obs THE MONOTONE WITNESS REDS ON A STALE BASE, and that is not a fault of these rows. It reads gaps_or_dupes=1 because %523 landed on xy while I worked and my base predates it; --next read 524 off the ANOINTED spine, which is the law, so 524 and 525 are correctly allocated and the gap closes on the rebase. Named here so a reader meeting the red mid-round knows which half is mine.
obs GRADE WHAT YOU TOUCH PUSHED ONE FRAME AND I WORKED IT DOWN. bron_resins_catalog_scan.sh read C+/76 -- register 54 on 46% negative sentences, reach 50 at grade 14 against 9. The header was dense and negative-led. Rewritten plainly it reads A/91 at grade 8, and the witness stayed green across the rewrite. The catalog itself reads 94, the witness 88, the widened shim_reason scan 88.
